  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EA28-2017 - Emergency and Early Recovery Program for Floods 2017 Affected People of Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EA 28/2017 has been launched in response to the devastating floods that have affected almost 6 million people in the Northern part of the country since 11 August. This proposed Emergency &amp; Early Recoveryprogramme, from August 2017 to June 2018 (nine months implementation, plus two months for preparation of final reports, external evaluation and audit), aims at covering the needs of 7,000 households (35,000 people in Bogra, Dinajpur, Jamalpur, Manikganj, Nowgoan and Thakugoandistricts) by ensuring their access to food and livelihoods (through unconditional cash, Cash for Work and agricultural inputsupport activities) as well as increasing their resilience via &#x201c;build back better&#x201d; Shelter (providing cash/training to 3,500 families for shelter repairing/construction).</narrative>
  </description>
